// ---- pedersen_step: one round of Stark Pedersen double-and-add ----------
// Computes:
//   if bit == 1 then ec_add(ec_double(running), base) else ec_double(running)
//
// This is the atomic round used to build up scalar multiplications in
// the full Pedersen hash. A 248-bit scalar mul is 248 unrolled rounds.
// The full Pedersen hash H(a, b) is 4 scalar muls (one per chunk of the
// two input felts, split 248/4 each) plus a shift point and 3 ec_adds
// to tie them together.

