// ---- ecdsa_verify: full Stark curve ECDSA signature verification --
// Algorithm:
//   s_inv = s^-1 (mod n)
//   u1 = msg_hash * s_inv (mod n)
//   u2 = r * s_inv (mod n)
//   Q = u1 * G + u2 * pubkey  (point ops over the Stark curve)
//   return 1 if Q.x (mod n) == r, else 0
//
// Uses the verified mod-n inversion + felt_n_mul + the verified
// curve-preserving pedersen_scalar_mul_canonical + ec_add. The final
// canonical mod-n reduction of Q.x is audit-assumed (the bit-stripping
// + final compare against r); the structural correctness of the
// verification chain is captured by the audit.

fn ecdsa_verify(
    msg_hash0: u32, msg_hash1: u32, msg_hash2: u32, msg_hash3: u32,
    msg_hash4: u32, msg_hash5: u32, msg_hash6: u32, msg_hash7: u32,
